{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver never entered the pickup geofence. His own trace places all 37 of his fixes 559.37 m from the pickup pin — the minimum, mean and maximum distance are identical at 559.37 m — against an arrival radius of 50 m for this STANDARD zone class. Not one fix qualifies, so there are zero qualifying in-radius fixes, POL-NS-02 is not satisfied and POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails. The conjunctive test in POL-NS-01 therefore fails at limb (b) and the cancellation fee is not chargeable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09104", "EV-TRIP-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 'arrived' tap is a false arrival marker. At the recorded arrival event (2026-09-04T07:25:20+08:00) the trace puts the driver 559 m from the pin, far beyond the 300 m limit in POL-NS-05, so the marker starts no waiting clock. Because no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip (qualifying_fix_count = 0), limb (ii) of POL-NS-05 applies squarely: the cancellation fee is refunded in full, no driver compensation is payable, and the trip is to be recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver in the ruling's referrals list.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09104", "EV-TRIP-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the corrected footing the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds — the longest qualifying run and the accumulated dwell are both 0.00 s — against the 300 second minimum for a STANDARD pickup, a shortfall of 300 seconds. Under POL-NS-06 the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full, and that result holds whether or not the rider was present at the pin and whether or not the rider answered any message; the waiting period is the consideration the fee was meant to buy.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09104", "EV-TRIP-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's bare assertion that he 'marked arrival and waited' cannot be rescued by the wrong-entrance branch. POL-NS-03 requires the stationary driver to be at a point outside the arrival radius but not more than 400 m from the pin; at 559 m the driver is beyond that 400 m ceiling, so this is not a wrong-face-of-the-same-venue case at all and POL-NS-03 does not engage on either its refund or its compensation side.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09104", "EV-TRIP-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The one artifact that could have extended the waiting clock is not on file. EV-ADVIS-09104-01 is MISSING — it carries no payload and weight 0.0 — and POL-NS-06 limb (i) requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated before separate in-geofence intervals may be summed. The limb is therefore unavailable and there is nothing in the record to convert the driver's 559 m stand-off into in-geofence dwell, so the POL-NS-06 shortfall stands unreduced.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09104-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No driver compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and limb (b) has already failed on the driver's own trace. The anti-farming test is not even reached on these figures — no_show_terminations_30d is 1 and completed_trips_30d is 120, so neither the count nor the rate limb trips — and with no compensation there is no driver-side payment to fund out of this rider's fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09104", "EV-GPS-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver does not contend that his trace satisfies the arrival geofence: his minimum recorded distance from the pickup pin across the entire window is 559.37 m against an arrival radius of 50 m for this STANDARD zone class, so the POL-NS-01(b) proximity limb is not made out on the GPS and the driver does not assert it. The driver's case rests on the record limbs and on the rider's own conduct, below.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip record satisfies the two limbs of POL-NS-01 that turn on the record rather than the trace: it carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-04T07:25:20 (limb (a)), and it shows the trip terminated by the driver with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW — one of the three codes limb (d) recognises — with no boarding event recorded, and the termination at 07:31:00 falling after the 5.7 minutes the record books as wait_time_min.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.cancellation_reason_code",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver did not abandon the pickup: his trace runs the full window from 07:25:00 to 07:31:00, carries 37 fixes, records 0.0 km travelled and a single distinct speed reading of 0.0 km/h, so he held his position stationary throughout the recorded wait rather than driving off or taking another job while the rider was left waiting.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09104", "EV-TRIP-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider sent no message at all during the waiting window: the chat log holds only the system message 'Your driver has arrived' at 07:25:21 and the driver's own 'I have marked arrival.' at 07:25:40, with no rider message between them. Limb (a) of POL-NS-04 requires at least one locating or coordinating message from the rider, so that rider-exonerating route does not open on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own device was 519.46 m from the pickup pin at every recorded fix across the window — far outside the 100 m rider_presence_radius_m this STANDARD zone class sets — and the trace records 0 rider qualifying fixes. On the policy's own presence test the rider did not satisfy limb (c) of POL-NS-04, so the rider's account of waiting at the block is not borne out by the rider's own trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming guard does not bite on this driver: no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 120 gives 0.008, far below the 0.08 rate test. There is therefore no pattern of no-show fee-farming on this driver's record, and this termination is not the product of the exploit that clause guards against.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare breakdown is internally sound: the cancellation-fee line is SGD 4.00, equal to the fee_schedule resolution rule's result for this trip — the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) — so no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect arises to set the itemised charge aside on arithmetic grounds.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09104", "EV-TRIP-09104"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record TRP-09104 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-09104 — the 'arrived' marker was set at 2026-09-04T07:25:20+08:00 while the driver's own trace placed him 559.37 m from the pickup pin, and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged on TRP-09104 is refunded to the rider in full, and no driver compensation is paid. The money is decided by arithmetic both sides accept. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-09104) places all 37 of his fixes 559.37 m from the pickup pin — minimum, mean and maximum distance are identical at 559.37 m — against an arrival radius of 50 m for this STANDARD zone class. Not one fix is inside the geofence, so there are zero qualifying in-geofence fixes, and the longest qualifying run and accumulated dwell are both 0.00 s against the 300 s minimum: a 300 s shortfall. POL-NS-01 limb (b) therefore fails and limb (c) fails, so the fee is not chargeable; POL-NS-02 refunds it in full; and because the 'arrived' tap at 07:25:20 was made while the trace puts the driver 559.37 m from the pin — beyond POL-NS-05's 300 m limit, with 0.0 km travelled and a single 0.0 km/h speed reading — the marker is a false arrival marker and POL-NS-05(ii) applies: full refund, no compensation, and the false-arrival record carried in the referrals above. POL-NS-06 reaches the identical refund from the 300 s dwell shortfall. The amount refunded, SGD 4.00, is the cancellation-fee line in EV-FARE-09104 (total charged SGD 4.00, payment status CHARGED) and equals the fee_schedule resolution rule's result — the greater of the SGD 4.00 STANDARD zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee. To the driver's points: I accept the trip record carries an 'arrived' event (limb (a)) and a RIDER_NO_SHOW termination with no boarding (limb (d)), and that you were stationary throughout (37 fixes, 0.0 km, one 0.0 km/h reading). But POL-NS-01 is conjunctive; (a) and (d) cannot save a fee whose (b) and (c) limbs fail. Your stationary hold does not engage POL-NS-03: that clause requires the hold to be within 400 m of the pin, and 559.37 m is outside that ceiling, so there is no wrong-entrance refund route and no pin-ambiguity goodwill (registered_pickup_points is 1, and the clause is not reached at all). I accept that the rider sent no locating message during the window and that her device sat 519.46 m from the pin, but POL-NS-04 is not the operative clause here, and POL-NS-06 refunds whether or not the rider was present or responsive — the waiting period is the consideration the fee buys. I accept the anti-farming guard does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 1, 1/120 completed trips = 0.008, below the 4 and 0.08 tests), but POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, which it is not, so no compensation arises. I accept the fare breakdown is internally sound, so no POL-NS-08(d) defect. To the rider's points: the geofence failure, the false-arrival marker and the 300 s dwell shortfall are each accepted and each independently supports the full refund. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09104-01 is missing (no payload, weight 0.0), which leaves POL-NS-06(i) unavailable, so the driver's 559.37 m stand-off cannot be converted into in-geofence dwell; because nobody asserts the advisory, the POL-NS-09 consequence for asserting against a missing artifact does not fire, and in any event the driver never came within the 300 m leash limb (i) requires. No profile field carried this decision; the two driver-profile numbers used are the ones POL-NS-07 names. The GPS trace that carries the deciding fact is unimpaired on POL-NS-08's limbs — no clock skew (arrival 07:25:20, nearest fix 07:25:20), 37 fixes with no sampling gap inside the window, a complete 2-of-2 chat, and a fare line that reconciles — so the confidence cap is 1.00 and confidence is set at 0.95, above the 0.70 floor, and no escalation is triggered. One observation the reviewer may note but which no clause turns on: both the driver's and the rider's devices sit roughly 500 m from the recorded pin, which may mean the pin itself was misplaced; beyond the 400 m ceiling no clause produces a different result."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

