    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 no-show fee charged on trip TRP-09104 is refunded in full to the rider.\n\nThe fee can stand only if all four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold, and condition (b) fails. The driver's own GPS trace, EV-GPS-09104, places him 559.37 m from the pickup pin at every one of his 37 fixes (min, mean and max are all 559.37 m), against the 50 m arrival radius for this STANDARD pickup. Not one fix falls inside the geofence, so there are zero qualifying in-radius fixes. Condition (c) fails too: the in-geofence dwell is 0 s against the 300 s minimum. POL-NS-02 therefore finds the driver never arrived and gives the rider a full refund of the cancellation fee.\n\nPOL-NS-05 puts the same conclusion beyond doubt on the false-arrival route. The driver's 'arrived' tap at 07:25:20 sits at a point 559 m from the pin, far beyond the 300 m limit, so the marker is FALSE and starts no waiting clock. Because no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip, POL-NS-05(ii) applies: the fee is refunded in full, no driver compensation is payable, and the trip is recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver (see referrals). POL-NS-06 agrees: on the corrected footing the effective dwell is 0 s, a 300 s shortfall, and the full refund holds whether or not the rider was present or answered messages.\n\nPOL-NS-03 does not engage. Its wrong-entrance branch requires the stationary driver to be within 400 m of the pin; at 559 m he is beyond that ceiling, so there is no pin-ambiguity goodwill of SGD 2.00 and no driver-side refund side to this case.\n\nOn the driver's claims: I accept that the trip record carries an 'arrived' event (POL-NS-01(a)) and a RIDER_NO_SHOW termination by the driver (limb (d)), but POL-NS-01 is conjunctive and fails at limbs (b) and (c). I accept that the trace shows the driver stationary at 0.0 km/h across the window — but that records him holding position 559 m from the pickup point, which satisfies no locating test and does not make the fee chargeable. His POL-NS-04 argument is correct and immaterial: the chat log (EV-CHAT-09104) holds only the system 'Your driver has arrived' message and the driver's own 'I have marked arrival.', with no locating message from the rider, so POL-NS-04 limb (a) is not met and that clause never opens; the rider's own device also sat 519.46 m from the pin (0 qualifying fixes, outside the 100 m radius), so limb (c) is not met either. The driver's POL-NS-07 anti-farming point is correct (no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below 4, and 1/120 = 0.008, below the 0.08 rate test), but compensation is not reached at all because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full; driver_compensation_sgd is therefore null, not the SGD 3.20 the fare model computes. The fare breakdown is sound: the SGD 4.00 cancellation line equals the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so no POL-NS-08(d) defect arises.\n\nOn the rider's claims: I accept the geofence, false-arrival, dwell and POL-NS-03 analysis above. Her own trace places her 519.46 m from the pin (0 qualifying fixes), but rider presence is not a condition of the refund under POL-NS-05(ii) or POL-NS-06, so it changes nothing. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09104-01 is MISSING (no payload, weight 0.0), so POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable and no separate in-geofence intervals can be summed; that limb could not have extended the clock.\n\nEvidence integrity (POL-NS-08): no artifact is impaired on limbs (a) to (d) — no clock skew (the 07:25:20 arrival matches a GPS fix), no trace gap (37 fixes, 0 s max gap, rider track present), no chat defect (2 messages equals trip_record.chat_message_count), no fare defect. POL-GEN-02 confidence is therefore capped at the weight of the trace that carries the deciding fact, EV-GPS-09104 at 1.0; the driver's statement that he 'marked arrival and waited' is not itself a carrier and does not rescue the fee. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is 0.95, the tap-versus-position conflict is resolved by POL-NS-05, there is no counterparty dispute history, no anti-farming trip (1 < 4), and the deciding fact rests on an unimpaired artifact. The fee is therefore refunded, not held."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
