    "explanation": "The SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged on TRP-09104 cannot stand, and I am refunding it in full to the rider.\n\nThe GPS trace (EV-GPS-09104) places the driver 559.37 m from the pickup pin at every one of his 37 fixes, from 07:25:00 to 07:31:00 — the minimum, mean and maximum distance are all 559.37 m, and there is not one in-geofence fix (qualifying_fix_count = 0). The pickup is STANDARD zone class, whose arrival radius under POL-NS-02 is 50 m. POL-NS-01 is conjunctive: all four conditions must hold, and limb (b) — GPS placement inside the geofence at or before the 'arrived' event — fails decisively. The 'arrived' tap at 07:25:20 therefore also fails under POL-NS-05: at that moment the driver was 559 m away, beyond the 300 m limit, so the marker is FALSE and starts no waiting clock. Because no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip, POL-NS-05(ii) governs — the fee is refunded in full and no driver compensation is payable. The same result follows from POL-NS-06: effective dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, a 300-second shortfall, and that clause refunds the fee whether or not the rider was present or responsive.\n\nTo the driver: I accept that you did not abandon the pickup. Your trace runs the full window, records a single speed reading of 0.0 km/h with 0.0 km travelled, the trip record carries the RIDER_NO_SHOW code, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming guard does not bite on you (no_show_terminations_30d = 1, below the count of 4, and 1/120 = 0.008, far below the 0.08 rate test). But POL-NS-01 requires GPS presence inside the geofence as well as a valid reason code, and at 559 m you were never at the pickup. For the same reason POL-NS-03 does not assist you: its wrong-entrance branch reaches only a driver stationary within 400 m of the pin, and 559 m is outside that ceiling, so neither its refund nor its goodwill side engages. No compensation is payable under POL-NS-07 because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full — the 80 percent figure would have been SGD 3.20 of the SGD 4.00 fee, but it is not earned here.\n\nTo the rider: you win the refund, but be clear about the record. Your own device reads 519.46 m from the pin across the window, outside the 100 m rider_presence_radius_m, and the chat log holds no locating message from you, so POL-NS-04 does not open and you do not need it — POL-NS-06 refunds the fee regardless of rider presence.\n\nThe missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09104-01, weight 0.0, no payload) cannot help the driver either: POL-NS-06(i) requires a present and populated advisory before separate in-geofence intervals may be summed, and there are no in-geofence intervals here to sum in any event.\n\nThe evidence I relied on is not impaired under POL-NS-08: the trace has no sampling gap (max_gap_sec 0.0) and well over six fixes across the window, the arrival timestamp coincides with a trace fix so there is no clock skew, the rider_track is present, the chat log matches trip_record.chat_message_count of 2, and the SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line equals the fee_schedule resolution rule (the greater of the SGD 4.00 STANDARD zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee), so no fare defect arises.\n\nBecause the false marker fired and no qualifying in-geofence fix exists, POL-NS-05(ii) directs that this trip be recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver; that instruction is carried in the referrals list."
  },
